-- title:
--   Transport of away-from-v units under conjugation by γ₀
-- statement:
--   Fix $a,b \in \mathbb{Q}$ and work in the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$. Let $R$ and $R'$ be $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which are orders in the sense of `IsOrder`, that is, each contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$. Let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, let $\gamma_0 \in \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]^\times$, and let $g$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ whose component at every height-one prime $w \neq v$ is trivial, in the sense that the base change [`Submodule.finiteAdeleEvalAt`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L36) of evaluation at $w$ sends $g$ to $1$. Assume moreover that [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31) applied to $R'$ and to the product of the diagonal image of $\gamma_0$ with $g$ equals $R$, i.e. $R$ is the submodule of elements of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ whose image in the adelic tensor product lies in $\beta \cdot \widehat{R'} \cdot \beta^{-1}$, where $\beta = (\gamma_0 \otimes 1)g$ and $\widehat{R'}$ is the adelic box of $R'$. The conclusion is that for every $x \in \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]^\times$ one has $x \in$ `awayUnits R v` if and only if $\gamma_0^{-1}x\gamma_0 \in$ `awayUnits R' v`, where `awayUnits Λ v` is the intersection, over all height-one primes $w \neq v$, of the preimages under the map on unit groups induced by $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \to$ `Loc a b w` of the subgroup generated by those units of `Loc a b w` which lie, together with their inverses, in the local box of $\Lambda$ at $w$.
--
--   This is the local–global bookkeeping step which says that an isomorphism of two orders' adelic boxes, realised by a global element $\gamma_0$ corrected by an idele supported at $v$, conjugates the groups of units that are integral at all primes away from $v$ into each other. It feeds the construction of the coset graph and of fake elliptic curves in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_CosetGraph_mem_awayUnits_iff_conj_mem_awayUnits_of_conjByFiniteIdele_finiteIdeleDiagonal_mul_eq.lean

